C port of upstream 2631bdf ("Support v0 demangling of trait object types with assoc
const bindings"): print_dyn_trait accepts `K<const>` after `p<ident>`; the C port
only parsed a type there, so the native_c differential fuzz target failed on any
symbol with an assoc const binding. The smoke_test case added here fails
without the demangle.c change.

Upstream: none found; crates/native-c at upstream HEAD (4023665) still lacks it.

diff --git a/crates/native-c/src/demangle.c b/crates/native-c/src/demangle.c
index 553d6b2..0752599 100644
--- a/crates/native-c/src/demangle.c
+++ b/crates/native-c/src/demangle.c
@@ -1505,7 +1505,11 @@ static NODISCARD overflow_status printer_print_dyn_trait(struct printer *printer
 
         PRINT_IDENT(printer, &name);
         PRINT_STR(printer, " = ");
-        PRINT(printer_print_type(printer));
+        if (printer_eat(printer, 'K')) {
+            PRINT(printer_print_const(printer, false));
+        } else {
+            PRINT(printer_print_type(printer));
+        }
     }
 
     if (open) {
